    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d394">

                <pb facs="0577" n="2041" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p2/pg2041"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.46E9/8–3151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Ceylon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Satterthwaite</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Colombo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-08-31T09:00:00+05:30">August 31, 1951—9
                            a. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>132. As result conversation reported my 130, Aug 30 Vaithianathan read me last
                    evening two ltrs which he said were ready for delivery.</p>
                <p>First was from PriMin to chairman Port Commission. Referring to latter’s oral
                    instrs from his departed Min to instruct oil cos furnish oil for Polish line
                    ships lifting rubber for China, ltr politely but clearly countermands these
                    orders. It states that in view oil shortage position oil cos is understandable
                    and that he shld therefore take no steps compelling them supply oil to such
                    ships.</p>
                <p>Second ltr was from Vaithianathan to director brokerage firm having principal
                    contract for rubber shipment in question who had written PriMin suggesting govt
                    shld take steps assist in obtaining bunkers for Polish vessels arriving to lift
                    rubber for China. Vaithianathan writes that he has been instructed by PriMin say
                    in reply that on acct shortage oil it would not be feasible do so.</p>
                <p>I expressed satis with action taken by PriMin. Emb will however continue fol
                    situation closely.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d394-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Dept pass London; sent Dept 132, rptd info London 37, Karachi 12, Delhi 18.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Satterthwaite</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d394-f1" n="1" xml:id="d394-f1-content">
                <p>On August 31, in response to telegrams 130 and 132 from Colombo, Assistant
                    Secretary McGhee congratulated Ambassador Satterthwaite on his handling of the
                    rubber discussions with the Prime Minister (telegram 86 to Colombo, not printed;
                    493.46E9/8–3151).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
